Description: Keep a constant frame rate on a still source when asked
 A compositor sends a new frame only when the screen changes. With
 PipeWireBaseEncodedStream::setConstantFramerate(true), the last frame that
 carries a picture is encoded again once per frame interval of
 maxFramerate() while no new frame comes, so a player of the live stream
 always gets its next picture; the encoder already gives a repeated frame
 its elapsed time (a10-reviewed-sender.patch). Off by default: a recording
 or a remote desktop session keeps sending frames on change only.
 Measured on a real Chromecast (Sparky Stereo OS, queue row 81, part D): a
 still desktop gave two pictures and then none, and the receiver buffered
 for ever; at a constant 30 frames a second it played. The repeat timer was
 made in initialize() with 100 ms, after start() had set the rate, so its
 first interval now follows the constant rate when it is on.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS
Forwarded: no
